<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95258" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκύθ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ</span>: voc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκύθᾰ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					829
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1112
			</span></i>, etc.:—<u>Scythian</u>, first in <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				55
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σκυθῶν ἐρημία</span>,
			of a desert, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				704
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>rude, rough person</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν λόγοις Σ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.847f
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				533.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Adj.
			<u>Scythian</u>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σ. ἐς οἷμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σ. ὅμιλος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				417
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίδηρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					818
				</span></i>
			 (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χάλυψ</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; κύανος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Lap.</u>
					55
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> at Athens,
				<i>one of the city police</i>, which was mainly composed of
			Scythian slaves, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				1018
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1026
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lys.</u>
				451
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοξότης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱπποτοξότης</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				2.13
			</span></i>.</div>
